Z||000000||Wannabe||02-06-2001||09:21 PM||||Anybody know if the taper of '88 ball joints is the same as the earlier joints?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||02-07-2001||04:55 PM||||They are not. Not only are they not, but the uppers can only be gotten from <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com." TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com.</A>  Check out Advance or AutoZone for the lowers.<P>They are also very expensive. I replaced all four for a total of almost $300  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (versus about $75 for all four on an early car!)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||02-07-2001||09:45 PM||||Figures. I suppose the Chevette bits weren't made to take much of a load. Ok, so here's the next question...which other GM ball joints DO have the same taper? Any ideas? Will, I don't suppose you still have the old ball joints kicking around? Condition would not be a concern as long as all the critical dimensions can be measured.<p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||02-07-2001||10:08 PM||||I've got a set of brand new still in the box upper ball joints for my '88. Haven't had a chance to install them. What measurements do you need. I've got a mic if that will suffice.<P>BTW, McQuay Norrice makes lower b/js for '88, for only $30/each.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||02-07-2001||11:41 PM||||Outstanding Fiero56! Here are the dimensions I need: 1.Width of mounting flange across the corners (the widest part) 2.Center to center distances between mounting holes <BR>3. Diameter of the base (the part that fits into the hole in the control arm)<P>That should give me enough info to see if I can move on to the next step. Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
